meta {
  name: List Products
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/products?page=1&limit=25&orderBy=desc
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  limit: 25
  orderBy: desc
  ~search: keyboard
}


vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
}

docs {
  # GET `/api/products`

  Retrieve a paginated list of products with optional search and sorting capabilities.

  ---

  ## Request

  **Method:** `GET`  
  **URL:** `/api/products`  
  **Authentication:** NONE

  ### Query Parameters

  | Parameter | Type | Required | Default | Description |
  |-----------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
  | `page` | `number` | No | `1` | Page number for pagination (minimum: 1). |
  | `limit` | `number` | No | `25` | Number of items per page (minimum: 1, maximum: 100). |
  | `orderBy` | `string` (`"asc"` \| `"desc"`) | No | `"desc"` | Sort direction by `createdAt` date. |
  | `search` | `string` | No | *undefined* | Case-insensitive search query matched against product `name` and `description`. |

  ---

  ## Responses

  ### `200 OK` — Products Retrieved Successfully

  Returned when products are successfully fetched according to pagination and search parameters.

  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "products retrieved successfully",
    "data": [
      {
        "id": "c7a8b9d0-1234-5678-9abc-def012345678",
        "name": "Wireless Mechanical Keyboard",
        "description": "Compact RGB wireless mechanical keyboard with tactile switches.",
        "price": 8999,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-03T12:00:00.000Z",
        "updatedAt": null,
        "deletedAt": null
      }
    ],
    "meta": {
      "correlationId": "req-abc123-xyz",
      "pagination": {
        "page": 1,
        "limit": 25,
        "totalRecords": 4,
        "totalPages": 1,
        "hasNextPage": false,
        "hasPrevPage": false
      }
    }
  }
  ```

  #### Response Data Shape & Data Types

  | Field | Type | Description |
  |-------|------|-------------|
  | `success` | `boolean` | Always `true` for successful responses. |
  | `message` | `string` | Status message (`"products retrieved successfully"`). |
  | `data` | `array` | List of product records matching criteria. |
  | `data[].id` | `string` (UUID v4) | Unique primary key identifier for the product. |
  | `data[].name` | `string` | Product title/name. |
  | `data[].description` | `string` | Detailed description of the product. |
  | `data[].price` | `number` (integer) | Price of the product in cents (e.g., `8999` represents $89.99). |
  | `data[].createdAt` | `string` (ISO 8601 Date) | Timestamp when the product record was created. |
  | `data[].updatedAt` | `string` (ISO 8601 Date) \| `null` | Timestamp when the product record was last updated, or `null`. |
  | `data[].deletedAt` | `string` (ISO 8601 Date) \| `null` | Timestamp when the product was soft-deleted, or `null`. |
  | `meta` | `object` | Metadata container. |
  | `meta.correlationId` | `string` | Unique identifier assigned to track the request lifecycle. |
  | `meta.pagination` | `object` | Pagination details. |
  | `meta.pagination.page` | `number` (integer) | Current page number. |
  | `meta.pagination.limit` | `number` (integer) | Max items per page. |
  | `meta.pagination.totalRecords` | `number` (integer) | Total matching product count. |
  | `meta.pagination.totalPages` | `number` (integer) | Calculated total pages available (`Math.ceil(total / limit)`). |
  | `meta.pagination.hasNextPage` | `boolean` | Indicates if subsequent pages exist (`page < totalPages`). |
  | `meta.pagination.hasPrevPage` | `boolean` | Indicates if previous pages exist (`page > 1`). |

  ---

  ### `401 Unauthorized` — Authentication Missing or Invalid

  Returned when the `Authorization` header is missing or contains an invalid/expired JWT token.

  ```json
  {
    "status": false,
    "error": {
      "code": "UNAUTHORIZED",
      "message": "Authentication token required"
    }
  }
  ```

  #### Response Shape

  | Field | Type | Description |
  |-------|------|-------------|
  | `status` | `boolean` | Always `false` for error responses. |
  | `error` | `object` | Error details object. |
  | `error.code` | `string` | Error code (`"UNAUTHORIZED"`). |
  | `error.message` | `string` | Description of authentication error. |

  ---

  ### `400 Bad Request` — Validation Error

  Returned when query parameters fail Zod schema validation (e.g. `page` < 1, `limit` > 100, `orderBy` invalid value).

  ```json
  {
    "status": false,
    "error": {
      "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
      "message": "Request validation failed",
      "details": [
        {
          "field": "query.limit",
          "message": "Number must be less than or equal to 100"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  ```

  #### Response Shape

  | Field | Type | Description |
  |-------|------|-------------|
  | `status` | `boolean` | Always `false` for error responses. |
  | `error` | `object` | Error details object. |
  | `error.code` | `string` | `"VALIDATION_ERROR"`. |
  | `error.message` | `string` | `"Request validation failed"`. |
  | `error.details` | `array` | List of field validation failures. |
  | `error.details[].field` | `string` | Target field path that failed validation. |
  | `error.details[].message` | `string` | Error message describing the rule violation. |

  ---

  ### `500 Internal Server Error` — Server Failure

  Returned when an unhandled server or database error occurs.

  ```json
  {
    "status": false,
    "error": {
      "code": "INTERNAL_ERROR",
      "message": "An unexpected error occured"
    }
  }
  ```

  #### Response Shape

  | Field | Type | Description |
  |-------|------|-------------|
  | `status` | `boolean` | Always `false` for error responses. |
  | `error` | `object` | Error container. |
  | `error.code` | `string` | `"INTERNAL_ERROR"`. |
  | `error.message` | `string` | Error description. |
}
